      "text": "The goal is to determine the product of several matrices, each of which is of the form\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & n \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix},\\]\nwhere \\( n = 1,3,5,\\ldots,99. \\)\n\nThe matrices are calculated by the exponent rule for powers of a matrix:\n\\[\n\\left( \\begin{array}{cc}\n1 & n\\\\{} \n0 & 1  \n\\end{array} \\right)^r =\n\\left( \\begin{array}{cc}\n1^n & n r\\\\{} \n0 & 1\n\\end{array} \\right).\n\\]\nSimilarly, we have \\(\\left( \\begin{array}{cc}\n1 & -n\\\\{} \n0 & 1  \n\\end{array} \\right)^s =\n\\left( \\begin{array}{cc}\n1^{-n} & -n s\\\\{} \n0 & 1\n\\end{array} \\right).\\]\n\nWe need to determine the product:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\dotsm \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 99 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{pmatrix} 1^n & 1 \\cdot 1\\\\{} \n0 & 1 \n\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1^{-1} & 1 \\cdot 1\\\\{} \n0 & 1 \n\\end{pmatrix} \\dotsm \\begin{pmatrix} 1^{{-99}} & 1 \\cdot 99\\\\{} \n0 & 1 \n\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nThis leads to:\n\\[\n\\bbox{1 to 99}.\n\\]",
